Hi,

TinnR automatically sets the wd to the path of the current script (if a file is opened) when starting R.
This is the greatest thing since sliced bread - I hate hate hate setting the directory manually when I'm just running a quick project.
Actually, I always hate it (Why backslashes in paths, MS-windows, why?) - I use the tag button quite a lot.
(Once again, TinnR is much more comfortable than Rstudio...)

Berry

PS: I want tinnR for Linux. Can I help pay someone for finally building it? Rstudio changes me into a nervous wreck.
I want window control, syntax highlighting, custom keyboard shortcuts (even for things like head, View, dim on F6,F7,F8), bookmarks, a setwd button, str on F2, the ability to send all lines untill the next empty line (with a personalized keystroke), control over which panel goes where (even on my second monitor), communication with several instances of R

